## Requirements

:::constraint{#C1 scope=document} Included files stay inside the workspace
No reader follows a path or link outside the allowed roots.
:::

:::requirement{#R1 priority=P0 status=accepted owner=@api-team} Section reads keep applicable instructions
Selecting a nested section returns every agent block and every constraint that applies to it.

:::acceptance{#AC1 test="../../core.test.ts"}
Given a document with an agent block in section 2
When an agent reads only section 3.1
Then the view holds the agent block
:::
:::

:::requirement{#R2 priority=P1 depends-on=R1} Budgets report what does not fit
:::

:::acceptance{#AC2 verifies=R2}
Given a budget below the required content
When the view is built
Then it ends with the overflow line
:::

:::constraint{#C2 applies-to=R2 level=should} Keep views under 2,000 tokens
:::

## Premises and evidence

:::assumption{#A1 owner=@maya review-by=2026-01-01} Most documents stay under 4,000 tokens
:::

:::evidence{#E1 supports=R1 method=test result=pass commit=1a2b3c4 date=2026-11-07 by=@ci}
The section-read tests pass.
:::

:::evidence{#E2 supports=R1 method=acceptance result=pass by=@maya date=2026-11-07}
Accepted after a review of the agent view.
:::

## Decisions

:::decision{#D1 status=superseded date=2026-10-01} Keep one cache for every reader
:::

:::decision{#D2 status=accepted date=2026-11-01 supersedes=D1 depends-on=R1} Give each reader its own cache
:::

## Questions

:::question{#Q1 status=open owner=@maya due=2026-12-01} Should constraints cost more than 500 tokens?
The budget pays for every document-scoped constraint.
:::

:::question{#Q2 status=answered between=C2,R2} Do C2 and R2 disagree?
:::

:::comment{for=Q2 kind=answer author=@maya date=2026-11-07} No
C2 is a should, so R2's overflow line still applies.
:::

## Tasks

- [x] Write the requirement blocks {#t1}
- [ ] Build the overflow line :depends[R2] {#t2}
- [ ] Measure the token cost :progress{basis=tasks}
